# Code owners — who OWNS each surface. This file is documentation, not a merge gate.
#
# "Require review from Code Owners" is deliberately OFF on this repo, and the required
# approving review count is 0 (see scripts/harden_github.py, which sets both and explains
# why: a sole code owner cannot approve their own pull request, so any nonzero count would
# deadlock every merge). A code-owner rule cannot fire under those settings, so nothing
# below blocks a merge on its own.
#
# What actually gates a merge here: a pull request is required, the CI status checks are
# required and must pass, and force-push/deletion on main are blocked. Treat the list below
# as "read this carefully before approving your own merge", not as an automatic stop.
#
# Sensitive surfaces = the places where tests can't save you (config, CI, secrets,
# self-executing code).

# Default owner for everything.
* @kphutt

# --- Sensitive paths: always human-reviewed --------------------------------
# CI / automation / anything self-executing on a runner.
/.github/        @kphutt
/scripts/        @kphutt
# Toolchain + supply-chain surfaces.
/pyproject.toml  @kphutt
/uv.lock         @kphutt
/.gitleaks.toml  @kphutt

# --- Engine surfaces (land with the v0.1 milestone) ------------------------
# The mutation-operator catalog + the GDScript adapter are the tool's real
# technical risk (a wrong mutant = a silently wrong survivor report). Keep reviewed.
/gdmutant/engine/            @kphutt
/gdmutant/engine/operators/  @kphutt
/gdmutant/adapters/          @kphutt
/gdmutant/cli.py             @kphutt
